{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KiZ51JNqXbChiG9A2R1gvJ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# ADR-012: Form-associated custom elements\n2\t\n3\t**Date:** 2026-11-24\n4\t\n5\t**Status:** Accepted\n6\t\n7\t**Related:** [ADR-004][adr-004] (client size)\n8\t\n9\t## Context\n10\t\n11\tA component author who wants to build a form control (a custom input,\n12\ta rich text field, a rating widget) cannot make it a real form control\n13\twith microtags. The platform way is a form-associated custom element:\n14\tthe class sets a static `formAssociated = true`, each host gets an\n15\t`ElementInternals` from `attachInternals()`, and the browser wires it\n16\tinto the containing form for submission, validation, and disabled\n17\tstate. Microtags calls `customElements.define` inside `setup()` with\n18\tno way to set the static first, and does not expose\n19\t`ElementInternals` to the setup callback.\n20\t\n21\tThe first consumer is `markdown-area`, a `<textarea>` replacement.\n22\t\n23\t## Decision\n24\t\n25\tA new builder link, `.formAssociated()`, opts a component into the\n26\tplatform's form-associated custom element behaviour. It takes no\n27\targuments.\n28\t\n29\t- **Builder link.** `.formAssociated()` returns a new builder with an\n30\t  internal `formAssociated` flag. The flag propagates through all\n31\t  subsequent links. It composes with `withProps`, `withRefs`,\n32\t  `withContexts` and `render` in any order.\n33\t\n34\t- **Static.** The factory sets `static formAssociated = true` on the\n35\t  generated class before the builder calls `customElements.define`,\n36\t  so the browser reads it at define time.\n37\t\n38\t- **Internals.** A form-associated host calls `attachInternals()`\n39\t  once, in its constructor. The result is kept on the instance and\n40\t  reused across disconnect/reconnect cycles. Setup receives it as\n41\t  `ctx.internals`.\n42\t\n43\t- **Setup context.** For a form-associated component the setup context\n44\t  gains `internals:ElementInternals`. Components that did not opt in\n45\t  get a type error when they read `ctx.internals`.\n46\t\n47\t- **Form lifecycle callbacks.** The class installs\n48\t  `formResetCallback`, `formDisabledCallback`,\n49\t  `formStateRestoreCallback` and `formAssociatedCallback` on the\n50\t  prototype. Each forwards to handlers registered through the\n51\t  `ctx.form(handlers)` method. The `restore` callback is replayed\n52\t  when a handler is registered; the others are not (their state is\n53\t  readable from the host and `internals`). Calling `ctx.form()` again\n54\t  replaces the earlier handlers. Handlers are dropped on teardown.\n55\t\n56\t- **Server render.** `render-support` is unchanged: form association\n57\t  has no server-side meaning.\n58\t\n59\t- **Types.** `FormAssociatedContext` is a public type export from\n60\t  `microtags`, so declaration emit in consuming packages does not hit\n61\t  TS2883. The builder carries a `FormAssoc` type parameter that\n62\t  controls whether the setup context includes `internals`.\n63\t\n64\t## Size cost\n65\t\n66\t| Entry | Before | After | Delta |\n67\t|-------|--------|-------|-------|\n68\t| `microtags` (core, ticket 02) | 4.04 kB | 4.09 kB | +50 B |\n69\t| `microtags` (core, ticket 03) | 4.09 kB | 4.23 kB | +140 B |\n70\t\n71\tThe ticket 02 delta (50 B) covers the `formAssociated` static, the\n72\t`attachInternals()` call in the constructor, and passing internals to\n73\tthe setup context. The ticket 03 delta (140 B) adds four prototype\n74\tcallbacks, `ctx.form()` with handler storage, and restore replay.\n75\tBoth are under the 150 B-per-ticket target.\n76\t\n77\t## Consequences\n78\t\n79\t- Authors can build form controls that submit values, participate in\n80\t  constraint validation, follow `disabled` from ancestor fieldsets,\n81\t  and hear about form reset and state restore.\n82\t- Components that do not opt in pay no runtime cost and no API change.\n83\t- The core entry limit rises from 4.1 kB to 4.25 kB.\n84\t\n85\t[adr-004]: ADR-004-client-bundle-size-outranks-ergonomics.md\n86\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_014UPCKmnimWAFbXhXsD2n9Y","agent_id":"a58061a4bd1065694","session_id":"6cc07e3d-f14d-4f74-8232-b688abdf9fde","uuid":"8f084d04-bf5b-4164-9410-5fa99d14114d","timestamp":"2026-11-24T09:58:15.903Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KiZ51JNqXbChiG9A2R1gvJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"fork","task_description":"Read key source files"}
