{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"a58061a4bd1065694","run_id":"0mwuiu80c-4518c9e8","tool_use_id":"toolu_014UPCKmnimWAFbXhXsD2n9Y","status":"completed","output_file":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-nick-code-microtags-form-associated-04-server-render-and-hydration/6cc07e3d-f14d-4f74-8232-b688abdf9fde/tasks/a58061a4bd1065694.output","summary":"Here's my report:\n\n---\n\n## File Survey for Ticket 04\n\n### `src/render-support.ts` (93 lines)\nServer render module. Exports `renderParts`, `renderHost`, `register`. **No form-associated awareness** -- it just serializes `RenderRecord` (tag, prop metas, ref names, render fn). Form association has no server meaning, confirming the ticket's expectation.\n\n### `src/builders.ts` (459 lines)\n`ComponentBuilder` has a `FormAssoc` type parameter (default `false`). `.formAssociated()` at line 316 returns a new builder with `formAssociated: true` in `BuilderConfig`. The `setup()` method (line 337) intersects the context type with `FormAssociatedContext` when `FormAssoc extends true`. The `formAssociated` flag is passed to `factory()` at line 349. The render link is set up at line 376 reading `c.renderFn` -- **completely independent of formAssociated**.\n\n### `src/factory.ts` (327 lines)\n- Constructor (line 112): conditionally calls `attachInternals()` and stores on `_internals`\n- `connectedCallback` (line 143): passes `this._internals` to `makeSetupContext` at line 206\n- `disconnectedCallback` (line 255): clears `_fh` on teardown\n- Lines 269-294: when `isFormAssociated`, defines `static formAssociated = true` on the class and installs four prototype callbacks (`formResetCallback`, `formDisabledCallback`, `formAssociatedCallback`, `formStateRestoreCallback`)\n\n### `src/build.ts` (573 lines)\nThe transform walks the AST for `.render()` calls in `define()` chains. It identifies `findChainRoot` by walking up property access chains to find `define(...)`. Key: it only looks for `.render` as a property access name -- **it doesn't care about other chain methods like `.formAssociated()`**. This is what I need to verify: that `.formAssociated().render()` and `.render().formAssociated()` (wait -- `.formAssociated()` returns a builder, and `.render()` also returns a builder, but `.setup()` is terminal) -- actually the chain root search walks through all intermediate `.method()` calls to find `define(...)`, so `.formAssociated()` in the chain should be transparent.\n\n### `test/ssr.ts` (872 lines)\ntapzero tests. No DOM. Imports `define` from source, `transform` from `src/build.js`. Pattern: `define('tag-name').withProps(...).render(...).setup(...)` then call `El.render(props)` / `El.renderParts(props)` and assert on the HTML string. No form-associated tests yet.\n\n### `test/index.ts` (3655 lines)\ntapzero browser tests. Form-associated tests at line 3242-3653 cover: FormData contribution, setValidity, :disabled in fieldset, ctx.internals.form, reconnect, composition with other links, non-opt-in unchanged, all lifecycle handlers. **No SSR/hydration tests for form-associated components yet** -- that's what this ticket adds.\n\n### `test/build.ts` (606 lines)\nTransform tests. Uses `transform()` directly and checks AST properties. No form-associated fixtures yet.\n\n### `test/preact-browser.ts` (162 lines)\nTests `toPreact` in browser. Uses `hydrate`/`render` from preact. No form-associated tests yet.\n\n### `test/fixtures/strip-render.ts` (7 lines)\nSimple fixture: `define('test-counter').render(...).setup(...)`. No `.formAssociated()`.\n\n### `.size-limit.js` (46 lines)\nCore limit: 4.25 kB. No change needed for this ticket (verification only).\n\n### `docs/adr/ADR-012-form-associated-components.md` (86 lines)\nRecords the decision. Notes \"Server render: render-support is unchanged.\"\n\n### Key Pattern for Tests\n- SSR tests run with `npm run test:ssr` (esbuild pipe to node)\n- Browser tests run with `npm test` (tapout, port 8123)\n- Transform tests run with `npm run test:build`\n- Preact tests: `npm run test:preact-ssr` and browser tests in `test/preact-browser.ts` (imported by `test/index.ts`)\n- Each test uses `test('name', t => { ... })` from `@substrate-system/tapzero`\n- Random tag names (`Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8)`) to avoid collisions","usage":{"total_tokens":98375,"tool_uses":16,"duration_ms":69618},"uuid":"6657a4c3-c949-4e34-8723-4c118d10cb48","session_id":"6cc07e3d-f14d-4f74-8232-b688abdf9fde"}
